<h2><a id="Exemples" name="Exemples"></a>Examples</h2>

<p>The following example shows the conversion of a DBF file containing information about a country's monumental trees.</p>

<div align="center">
<table>
<tr>
<td><div align="center"><img src="DBFCSV_exemple_taula.png"/></div></td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td align="center">Tabla DBF origen</td>
</tr>
</table>
</div>

<p>If the semicolon (;) is used as the separator, the header and the first row of data from the original DBF table containing the monumental trees are written as follows:</p>

<pre>ID_GRAFIC;MENA_DECLA;NOM_DECLAR;ESPECIE;INE;TERME_MUNI;COMARCA;MATRICULA;ESTAT_DETA;ESTAT_RESU;URL;COORX;COORY;OBJECTID
0;AM;Pi Vell de l'Arp II;Pinus uncinata;25909;Vansa i Fórnols, La;Alt Urgell, l';AM 04.909.01b;N;Viu;http://mediambient.gencat.cat/ca/05_ambits_dactuacio/patrimoni_natural/arbres-monumentals/am_arbres_monumentals_fitxes/alt-urgell-6/pins-vells-de-larp-l-ll-lll/;377432.00;4673067.00;26 
</pre>

